'''''Kalanchoe tetraphylla''''' is a species of ''[[Kalanchoe]]'' native to [[Madagascar]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=''Kalanchoe tetraphylla'' H.Perrier |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:274499-1 |access-date=2024-12-02 |website=Plants of the World Online |publisher=Kew Science}}</ref> It is a small [[shrub]] with a simple stout stem and usually two pairs of opposite leaves, closely related to ''[[Kalanchoe synsepala]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |title=''KALANCHOE TETRAPHYLLA'' H.Perrier, 1923 |url=https://www.crassulaceae.ch/de/artikel?akID=68&aaID=2&aiID=T&aID=3171 |access-date=2024-12-02 |website=International Crassulaceae Network}}</ref> Its scientific name is often misapplied by [[horticulturist]]s to the continental southern African species ''[[Kalanchoe luciae]]''.

